{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton G1 models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes (uncontrollable) from motion commands (controllable). The specification automata E1-E4 bind each perception outcome to a unique, safe, and efficient action, enforcing deterministic recovery from obstacles and systematic exploration. E5 prevents repeated identical actions to promote coverage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
    "Use one specification per perception-to-action binding, plus an alternation spec to avoid repeated actions and promote coverage."
  ],
  "G": [
